hat would happen to each file without changing anything\n  --versions <folder>    Keep replaced or removed files in that destination folder\n  --skip-junk            Skip Thumbs.db, desktop.ini, .DS_Store, ~$...\n  --smb-compress         Ask for SMB compression when copying over the network (slow networks)\n  --atomic               All or nothing: the folder only appears when it is complete\n  --rescue               Rescue mode: save what is readable from a damaged disk (unreadable parts as zeros)\n  --delta                When replacing large files, write only the blocks that changed\n  --organize             Organize photos and videos into year-month folders by capture date\n  --skip-duplicates      Do not copy what is already in the destination (same content, any name)\n  --encrypt              Encrypted copy with a password (AES-256, .mcenc files)\n  --crash-after-mb <n>   [test] Kill the process after confirming n MB of a file\n\nCtrl+C pauses the transfer; 'resume' continues from the last confirmed block.",
